---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TimeLineElement from "../components/cv/TimeLine.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Resume">
  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-2xl w-full font-bold">Curriculum Vitae</div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10 text-justify text-base">
    <p class="mb-3">
      Robotics engineer specializing in safety-critical autonomy for real-world robotic systems.
      At Toyota Research Institute of North America (TRINA), I build real-time planning and control
      systems for autonomous maneuvering of articulated vehicles, combining model-based optimization
      (MPPI/MPC) with diffusion-inspired trajectory sampling.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-3">
      Previously, I developed SIL/HIL simulation pipelines for ADAS validation at Nikola Corporation,
      and built real-time adaptive safety controllers for physical human-robot interaction at
      Honda Research Institute.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-3">
      My research on neural network repair — where learned control policies are formally corrected
      to satisfy safety constraints via mixed-integer optimization — has been published at CoRL, ICRA,
      IROS, and received a Best Workshop Paper Award at NeurIPS 2022. I have also contributed to
      risk-bounded control using stochastic barrier functions, behavior-aware motion planning for
      collaborative robots, and the Open X-Embodiment large-scale robot learning dataset.
    </p>
    <p>
      Ph.D. in Computer Science from Arizona State University (co-advised by
      <a href="http://henibenamor.weebly.com">Heni Ben Amor</a> and
      <a href="http://fainekos.net">Georgios Fainekos</a>),
      M.Sc. in Electrical Engineering from North Carolina A&T State University,
      and B.Sc. from Ferdowsi University of Mashhad.
      Full CV is available <b><a href="/cvs/resume_keyvan_majd.pdf">here</a></b>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-2xl w-full font-bold">Education</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container grid gap-4 mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Arizona State University | 2019 - 2024"
      subtitle="Ph.D. in Computer Science (GPA: 4.0/4.0)"
      desc1="Thesis: Safe Robot Learning with Neural Network Repair"
      desc2="Co-advisors: Prof. Heni Ben Amor and Prof. Georgios Fainekos"
    />
    <TimeLineElement
      title="North Carolina A&T State University | 2017 - 2019"
      subtitle="M.Sc. in Electrical Engineering (GPA: 4.0/4.0)"
